checks_run.procedure:
Write an adversarial probe that imports the CANDIDATE's schedule-explained.mjs from the clone. Feed explain(), gate0() and stage() inputs modelled on the real DO-D9 quarter2 report, mutating one condition at a time to make the rule explain writes it must not:
- an initiating user, or run_as user;
- an event trigger;
- an unscheduled code, a disabled schedule, or two enabled rows for one code;
- a key naming another schedule;
- a slot before or after the window, a key minute off the cron, an S7 boundary at exactly W0-60 s, an unknown timezone, an unsupported cron, or an invalid date;
- a second execution per slot (listed, or only a peer);
- created_at outside the window;
- events with a user, on behalf of a user, from the api, a non-job request id, or at or below the baseline;
- a version mismatch;
- results without or with a foreign job event, a stray result, a result of a package execution, a late attempt, or two starter results;
- for Gate 0: an unrelated table, a line after the final line, unexplained changed keys, missing rows, child_of basis, a hidden table count, attachment differences, exit 1, no final line, 20 keys, expected-but-not lines, unknown lines, a duplicate table line, results only, an orphan key line, or user_identity.
The probe exits 1 on any deviation.
